1475","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch16_quadratic_form_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What information is lost if one only evaluates $v^TAv$ at standard basis vectors?","options":["The trace of $A$, the sum of its diagonal entries","The diagonal entries $a_{ii}$ of the matrix $A$","Possible cross-term behaviour between coordinates","The value of the form at scaled vectors such as $2e_1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"08100f1affaae9f4fa7a8c9a","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch16_quadratic_form_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which symmetric matrix corresponds to $q(x,y,z)=x^2+2xy+4xz+3z^2$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1&1&2\\\\1&0&0\\\\2&0&3\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&1&4\\\\1&0&0\\\\4&0&3\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&4\\\\0&0&0\\\\0&0&3\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1&2\\\\1&1&0\\\\2&0&3\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cbd963e8203284d3a18c4b4b","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch16_quadratic_form_010_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A quadratic form satisfies $Q(\\boldsymbol{v})=3$ for some vector $\\boldsymbol{v}$. What is $Q(-2\\boldsymbol{v})$?","options":["$12$","$-12$","$-6$","$6$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"759b17fe16f9b0466c699ab0","time_limit":20}]}}